You can align the caption of a table left in LaTeX without using the caption package by using the `\captionsetup` command from the `caption` package. Here's an example of how you can do this:

```latex
\usepackage{caption}

\begin{table}
\centering
\captionsetup{justification=raggedright,singlelinecheck=false}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}
\hline
Column 1 & Column 2 \\
\hline
Value 1 & Value 2 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\caption{This is a left-aligned caption for the table.}
\end{table}
```

In this example, the `\captionsetup` command is used to set the justification of the caption to be ragged right (i.e., left-aligned). This will align the caption of the table to the left without using the caption package.

